      "num_turns": 39,
      "result": "Implemented the Rails URL shortener API with PostgreSQL persistence, unique short codes, click tracking, JSON error responses, and an executable `start.sh` that migrates and serves on `0.0.0.0:8000`. Startup instructions are in the README.\n\nVerified the API over HTTP: creation (including generated codes), duplicate and invalid inputs, malformed JSON, listing, lookup, redirects, 404s, and click counts surviving a server restart. The test records were removed afterward, and the server is stopped so `sh start.sh` can be run cleanly.\n\nI also pinned JSON to the compatible 2.x series because Rails 8.0’s encoder is incompatible with JSON 3.x.",
